{"id":"9ed2205613da2248","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map.md","title":"ZFC Measure7 Conditional Expectation Map","display":"df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map — ZFC Measure7 Conditional Expectation Map","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map","aliases":["58-df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map"],"display":"df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map — ZFC Measure7 Conditional Expectation Map","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-zfc-prob-conditional-expectation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-measure7-conditional-expectation-map — ZFC Measure7 Conditional Expectation Map"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d139c8e88761c759\" href=\"?note=d139c8e88761c759\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-zfc-prob-conditional-expectation.md\">../batch09/58-df-zfc-prob-conditional-expectation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal G,\\mu,f,g\\in V\">\\(X,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal G,\\mu,f,g\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (measure-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md\">../batch12/58-df-measure-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (sub-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"a740bdad87b97ac6\" href=\"?note=a740bdad87b97ac6\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md\">../batch07/58-df-sigma-algebra.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IntegrableReal}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{IntegrableReal}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> (representative-level integrability and measurability predicates, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d139c8e88761c759\" href=\"?note=d139c8e88761c759\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-zfc-prob-conditional-expectation.md\">../batch09/58-df-zfc-prob-conditional-expectation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7ConditionalExpectationMap}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7ConditionalExpectationMap}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure7\\text{-}conditional\\text{-}expectation\\text{-}map}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7ConditionalExpectationMap}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal G,\\mu,f,g)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)\\land\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\mathcal A\n\\land\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G,X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{IntegrableReal}_S(f,X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{IntegrableReal}_S(g,X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal G),(\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)))\n\\land\\forall E\\in\\mathcal G\\;\\left(\\int_Eg\\,d\\mu=\\int_Ef\\,d\\mu\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}measure7\\text{-}conditional\\text{-}expectation\\text{-}map}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure7ConditionalExpectationMap}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mathcal G,\\mu,f,g)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)\\land\\mathcal G\\subseteq\\mathcal A\n\\land\\operatorname{SigmaAlgebra}(\\mathcal G,X)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{IntegrableReal}_S(f,X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)\n\\land\\mathrm{IntegrableReal}_S(g,X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(g;(X,\\mathcal G),(\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R)))\n\\land\\forall E\\in\\mathcal G\\;\\left(\\int_Eg\\,d\\mu=\\int_Ef\\,d\\mu\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This representative-level definition works for an arbitrary measure space; integrability and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal G\">\\(\\mathcal G\\)</span>-measurability are delegated to the existing typed predicates rather than reconstructed with hidden inverse-image notation.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnch